00:00:14,244 --> 00:00:19,843
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

5
00:00:19,893 --> 00:00:22,342
اَلْحَمْدُلِلَّهِ اَوَّلاً وَآخِرًا

6
00:00:23,406 --> 00:00:29,318
اَلَّلهُمَّ اِنَّ نَحْمَدُكَ حَتَّى تَرْضَى وَ نَحْمَدُكَ عِنْدَ الرِّضَى وَ نَحْمَدُكَ بَعْدَ الرِّضَى

7
00:00:30,047 --> 00:00:35,854
وَنُصَلِّيْ وَنُصَّلِّمْ عَلَى سَيِّدِ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَالْآخِرِيْنَ وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

8
00:00:36,453 --> 00:00:38,640
اَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمةُ الله وَبَرَكَاتُه

9
00:00:39,714 --> 00:00:44,955
When the Armies disbanded, after the Battle of the trench,

10
00:00:45,753 --> 00:00:54,649
The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Now, we will attack them, they will not attack us.

11
00:00:55,095 --> 00:00:58,412
اَلْآنَ نَغْزُوهُمْ وَلاَ يَغْزُونَنَا

12
00:00:59,587 --> 00:01:04,841
This marked the turning point in the Islamic history, of the new founded state

13
00:01:05,516 --> 00:01:10,036
for the past five years the Muslims were engaged in a defensive battle with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

14
00:01:10,969 --> 00:01:13,031
defensive battle for survival.

15
00:01:13,703 --> 00:01:18,505
Now, the tables are turned, it is Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), that will be struggling to survive,

16
00:01:19,052 --> 00:01:24,338
it will be Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) who will, now be on the defensive.

17
00:01:25,302 --> 00:01:27,674
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are the ones who attack the Muslims in Badr(بدر),

18
00:01:28,691 --> 00:01:30,872
it was Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), who attacked in Uhud(أحَد),

19
00:01:31,493 --> 00:01:34,022
it was Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) who attacked in Al-Khandaq(الخندق)

20
00:01:34,503 --> 00:01:36,153
and that was their last attempt.

21
00:01:36,909 --> 00:01:39,664
That was not because they were having a change of heart

22
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:44,900
or because they were now, somehow becoming more sympathetic of the Muslims,

23
00:01:45,283 --> 00:01:47,535
 it was simply because they were exhausted

24
00:01:48,095 --> 00:01:51,095
they couldn't carry on this fight, any further.

25
00:01:51,923 --> 00:01:56,122
The Muslims have out done them in patience, and perseverance

26
00:01:56,553 --> 00:01:58,700
and they couldn't keep up with them.

27
00:01:59,071 --> 00:02:02,770
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ  would say a year from now as we will see

28
00:02:03,230 --> 00:02:05,425
when we're talking about Al-Hudaybiyya(ألحديبية).

29
00:02:05,614 --> 00:02:08,326
يَا وَيْحَ قُرَيْشٍ لَقَدْ أنهكتهم الْحَرْبَ

30
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:11,237
Woe to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), war has exhausted them.

31
00:02:11,768 --> 00:02:15,610
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in Surat Al-Imran(سورة العمران), in the last Ayah(آية),

32
00:02:16,005 --> 00:02:23,442
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اصْبِرُوا وَصَابِرُوا وَرَابِطُوا

33
00:02:23,768 --> 00:02:29,971
وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ۝

34
00:02:31,141 --> 00:02:32,606
 Isbiroo(إِصْبِرُوْا) means, be patient,

35
00:02:32,671 --> 00:02:40,504
Sabiroo (صَابِرُوْا) in Sarf(صرف) in Arabic in the science of, what is called Sarf(صرف),

36
00:02:40,985 --> 00:02:45,925
looks at the components of the word or the makeup of the word,

37
00:02:46,415 --> 00:02:48,703
you see in the Ayah(آية) it says: Isbiroo(إصْبِرُوْا) Wa-Sabiroo(وَصَابِرُوْا),

38
00:02:49,208 --> 00:02:53,393
Isbiroo(إصْبِرُوْا) Wa-Sabiroo(وَصَابِرُواْ) they both come from the same root word which is Sabr(صَبْر)

39
00:02:53,806 --> 00:02:55,950
but (إصْبِرُوْا) is a command to be patient.

40
00:02:56,166 --> 00:02:57,223
So, what is Sabiroo (صَابِرُوْا)?

41
00:02:57,645 --> 00:03:01,690
Sabiroo( صَابِرُوْ) is in the Wazan(وَزَنْ) what they call the Wazan(وَزَنْ) of Mufaela(مفاعلة),

42
00:03:02,626 --> 00:03:04,626
it is patience between two parties.

43
00:03:05,355 --> 00:03:10,428
So, in Arabic for example, you have Musaria(مسارعه), Mudhariba(مضاربه), Muqatila(مقاتله)

44
00:03:11,007 --> 00:03:17,585
here the Fael(فعل) the verb is not done by individual but it's between two parties.

45
00:03:18,153 --> 00:03:22,153
So, as if Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling us that even though you might be patient

46
00:03:22,606 --> 00:03:27,038
but what if your enemy is more patient then you, you have to outdo them and patience,

47
00:03:27,118 --> 00:03:29,149
so you have in the Ayah(آية) two commands from Allah,

48
00:03:29,189 --> 00:03:33,222
one of them is to be patient and the other one is to outdo your enemy in patience,

49
00:03:33,324 --> 00:03:34,531
Isbiroo(إصْبِرُوْا) Wa-Sabiroo(وَصَابِرُوْا).

50
00:03:35,126 --> 00:03:38,999
And that is what the Muslims did and it paid off, now.

51
00:03:39,929 --> 00:03:43,080
After Badr(بدر) and Uhud(أحَد) and Al-Khandaq(ألخندق),

52
00:03:43,336 --> 00:03:52,447
now it is Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) who will be on the defensive because the Muslims wore them out, the Muslims tired them.

53
00:03:53,046 --> 00:03:54,701
 And now Rasool Allah ﷺ  is saying;

54
00:03:54,774 --> 00:03:56,540
 اَلْآنَ نَغْزُوهُمْ وَلاَ يَغْزُونَنَا

55
00:03:56,981 --> 00:04:01,120
Now, we will conquer them, they will not conquer us, we will not attack them, they will not attack us.

56
00:04:02,274 --> 00:04:07,091
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) was never again, able to bring together an army to invade Madina

57
00:04:07,131 --> 00:04:12,281
 that's it, he has done his best, to the extent that he was able,

58
00:04:12,551 --> 00:04:17,281
same with his people, his followers in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), that was the best they could pull off.

59
00:04:17,583 --> 00:04:20,268
 The 10,000 strong army of Al-Khandaq(ألخندق).

60
00:04:20,927 --> 00:04:30,547
It was a failure in the end because of the supernatural events that occurred, the wind and the soldiers of Allah.

61
00:04:30,594 --> 00:04:32,614
وَمَا يَعْلَمُ جُنُودَ رَبِّكَ إِلَّا هُوَ

62
00:04:32,639 --> 00:04:38,169
Only Allah knows His soldiers, we don't know the soldiers of Allah, anything can be a soldier of Allah.

63
00:04:39,052 --> 00:04:45,639
Sometimes things that are blessings, things that they are the reasons for life, could be a soldier of Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

64
00:04:45,679 --> 00:04:49,498
 like water for example was a soldier of Allah, it killed Firaoun(فرعون),

65
00:04:49,712 --> 00:04:52,783
 a mosquito killed Namrood(نمرود),

66
00:04:53,173 --> 00:04:55,820
the earth swallowed up Qaroon(قارون),

67
00:04:55,971 --> 00:05:00,622
wind is a soldier of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, it destroyed nations, thunderbolts.

68
00:05:00,876 --> 00:05:08,333
 So, anything in this universe can be a soldier of Allah, we don't know soldiers of Allah that are around us.

69
00:05:09,228 --> 00:05:17,257
With this the Muslims ended a very difficult period of defending their mere existence and holding on to their base.

70
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:24,020
The Muslims even though we say that the establishment of the Islamic State was with Hijrah(هجرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

71
00:05:24,187 --> 00:05:32,327
 but those were very, very difficult days the initial years in Madina were years of fear, were years of hiding, were years of insecurity.

72
00:05:32,446 --> 00:05:36,565
 We shouldn't think that this was a flourishing strong Islamic State,

73
00:05:36,621 --> 00:05:43,761
 it was in a very difficult, predicament, Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) from one side the Yahood(يهود) from the other,

74
00:05:43,809 --> 00:05:47,740
the Bedouins from the third, very difficult time on the Muslims.

75
00:05:47,832 --> 00:05:53,653
Sahabah(صحابه) used to say we would sleep with our arms next to us, we wouldn't feel security.

76
00:05:54,226 --> 00:05:57,200
So, these first five years were very difficult,

77
00:05:57,939 --> 00:06:02,117
but the Muslims held on strong, they have Sabr(صبر) in Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

78
00:06:02,704 --> 00:06:06,674
But now the Muslims will move on to occupy new positions.

79
00:06:07,177 --> 00:06:10,346
The next five years are going to be years of expansion,

80
00:06:10,927 --> 00:06:16,100
the move from the defensive Jihad(جهاد) to the offensive one has taken place.

81
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:23,661
In these next five years, dear brothers and sisters, we will see an exponential growth of Islam

82
00:06:24,150 --> 00:06:26,525
and some important events occurring.

83
00:06:26,884 --> 00:06:29,674
The key events which we will talk about In sha Allah Ta'ala(اِنْشاءالله تعالى),

84
00:06:29,747 --> 00:06:37,344
we ask Allah to give us the ability to go through the remainder of the five years of Seerah(سيرة), and to make this beneficial.

85
00:06:37,672 --> 00:06:40,427
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to give us beneficial knowledge.

86
00:06:40,486 --> 00:06:44,142
اَلَّهُمَّ اِنَّا نَسْالُكَ عِلْمًا نَافِعَ وَ نَعَوْذُبِكَ مِنَّ عِلْمِ لَّايَنْفَعُ

87
00:06:44,578 --> 00:06:46,356
These key events are going to be the,

88
00:06:46,649 --> 00:06:49,616
Truce of Al-Hudaybiyya(ألحديبية) and the sixth year of Hijrah(هجرة),

89
00:06:50,047 --> 00:06:52,893
the Battle of Khaybar(خيبر) and the seventh year of his Hijrah(هجرة).

90
00:06:53,172 --> 00:06:55,756
The Battle of Maota(موته), the opening of Makkah,

91
00:06:55,780 --> 00:06:58,794
The Battle of Hunain(حنين) and At-At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف) in the eighth year,

92
00:06:59,090 --> 00:07:03,347
and then the Battle of Tabook(تبوك) and the farewell Hajj(حَجْ), in the ninth year.

93
00:07:03,973 --> 00:07:13,151
And finally, the greatest event of all, the greatest, calamity that has ever befell, the Muslim Ummah(امة)

94
