97
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:38,319
We talked in the previous set of lectures, about the assassination of Ka'ab Ibn Ashraf(كعب إبن أشرف)

98
00:07:38,797 --> 00:07:42,080
and we said that Ka'ab Ibn Ashraf(كعب إبن أشرف) was a Jewish leader,

99
00:07:42,295 --> 00:07:50,970
very rich man held an important position, among the people in Hijaz(حجاز), and he was a very eloquent poet

100
00:07:51,238 --> 00:07:53,512
and he used to use this poetry,

101
00:07:53,758 --> 00:07:56,108
and poetry we talked about the importance of it,

102
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:59,804
in the days of Jahilliyah(جاهلية), it was the media of the day

103
00:08:00,438 --> 00:08:07,960
and Ka'ab Ibn Ashraf(كعب إبن أشرف) would use this poetry of his, to defame the Muslims and talk against Rasool Allah ﷺ.

104
00:08:08,309 --> 00:08:12,124
If one would read in the history of the Jahilliyah(جاهلية) in Arabia,

105
00:08:12,528 --> 00:08:19,023
one would see that a particular line of history would bring a ruin to a tribe, it would ruin their reputation.

106
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:25,535
Just like a documentary or, or a particular article in The Big newspaper would do today.

107
00:08:26,004 --> 00:08:29,474
 In fact, probably even the effect of poetry was greater.

108
00:08:30,028 --> 00:08:37,117
So, Ka'ab Ibn Ashraf(كعب إبن أشرف), one of the things he was doing he was even talking about the Muslim women and Muslims then,

109
00:08:37,514 --> 00:08:40,022
 and this should be the case with the Muslims all the time,

110
00:08:40,456 --> 00:08:45,644
should stand up, for the rights of Al-Muslimaat(ألمسلمات) and defend Al-Muslimaat(ألمسلمات),

111
00:08:45,737 --> 00:08:50,087
and we know of many, stories in our history of that occurring

112
00:08:50,127 --> 00:08:55,190
for example the Battle of Bannu Qainuqah(بنوقينقاع), against the Jewish tribe of Bannu Qainuqah(بنوقينقاع) in Madina was

113
00:08:55,267 --> 00:09:01,729
because of their attack on a Muslim woman, when they uncovered her

114
00:09:02,043 --> 00:09:08,764
 and we know what happened with Al-Motasim(ألمعتصم), the Muslim Khalifah(خليفه) in Daulat-Al-Abbasia(ألدولة العباسيهِ),

115
00:09:09,246 --> 00:09:12,976
when the woman called to him Wa-Motasimah(وا معتصماہ) when the Romans attacked.

116
00:09:13,524 --> 00:09:16,794
Then he mobilize an entire army to go and defend her.

117
00:09:17,371 --> 00:09:21,393
So, Ka'ab Ibn Ashraf(كعب إبن أشرف) was speaking against Muslim women

118
00:09:21,786 --> 00:09:27,064
and it's said that he has spoken about Umm Al-Fadhal(أم الفضل),

119
00:09:27,104 --> 00:09:30,695
the wife of Al-Abbas Bin Abdul-Muttalib(ألعباس بن عبدالمطلب), the uncle of Rasool Allah ﷺ .

120
00:09:31,009 --> 00:09:33,612
 Anyway, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

121
00:09:33,652 --> 00:09:37,168
مَنْ لِّيْ بِكَعْب اِبْنِ اَشْرَفْ فَاِنَّه’قَدْ آذَّى اللهَ وَ رَسُوْله

122
00:09:37,567 --> 00:09:43,047
Who will get rid of Ka'ab Ibn Ashraf(كعب إبن أشرف) because he has harmed Allah and His messenger.

123
00:09:43,739 --> 00:09:53,029
Muhammad Ibn Maslima رضي الله عنه volunteered, for this special operation along with some other members of his tribe.

124
00:09:53,661 --> 00:09:54,957
What tribe was this?

125
00:09:55,184 --> 00:09:57,413
This tribe was Al-Aos(ألأوس).

126
00:09:57,782 --> 00:10:01,189
So, it was a Al-Aos(ألأوس) who killed Ka'ab Ibn Ashraf(كعب إبن أشرف).

127
00:10:01,825 --> 00:10:06,657
Now, as one of Al-Ansaar(ألانصار) or the one of the descendants of Al-Ansaar(ألانصار) said:

128
00:10:07,287 --> 00:10:09,229
In a narration mentioned by Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر)

129
00:10:09,735 --> 00:10:16,610
that Al-Aos Wal Khazraj(اَلْأوس وَالْخزْرج) were like two stallions, competing in front of Rasool Allah ﷺ .

130
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:21,957
Whenever, one clan would do something in service of Rasool Allah ﷺ ,

131
00:10:22,221 --> 00:10:28,231
the other clan would not want them to take that advantage alone, and would try to do something similar.

132
00:10:28,557 --> 00:10:30,986
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), we see that they had competition,

133
00:10:31,391 --> 00:10:34,241
they had this spirit of competition, but it wasn't in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا),

134
00:10:34,509 --> 00:10:37,181
it wasn't and who would be more successful in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا),

135
00:10:37,374 --> 00:10:41,644
who would make more money, who would hold a higher position,

136
00:10:42,009 --> 00:10:49,556
as we see competition now, in the material world in the materialistic, capitalistic world

137
00:10:49,983 --> 00:10:52,578
and way of life that the West is promoting.

138
00:10:52,848 --> 00:10:56,637
You know, the success philosophy, in the West today

139
00:10:56,999 --> 00:11:04,989
and the competition for success that the West is presenting to the world today, is a materialistic one.

140
00:11:05,744 --> 00:11:11,727
And it holds no value in the Islamic view of things.

141
00:11:12,267 --> 00:11:17,966
Because success in the West is defined in, purely materialistic terms.

142
00:11:18,368 --> 00:11:24,917
But the success in Islam is how close to Allahعَزّوجَلّ you are?

143
00:11:25,218 --> 00:11:31,558
So, a person could be totally unknown in Duniya(دنيا), he could be very poor,

144
00:11:31,993 --> 00:11:37,371
nevertheless, he is very successful because he's close to Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

145
00:11:37,739 --> 00:11:41,914
And a classical example that one could give of that is Al-Owais Al-Qarni(إويس ألقرني).

146
00:11:42,278 --> 00:11:48,205
I mean Owais Al-Qarni(إويس ألقرني) , was a person that was ambiguous, people didn't know him.

147
00:11:48,435 --> 00:11:54,246
And when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) ask the delegation that came from the tribe of Owais Al-Qarni(إويس ألقرني)

148
00:11:54,305 --> 00:11:57,733
 the name of his tribe was Muraad(مراد), it's a tribe in Yemen.

149
00:11:58,145 --> 00:12:00,843
And when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) asked about him, they said

150
00:12:00,883 --> 00:12:05,785
(I mean, the way they talked about him is, as if they were surprised, why the Ameer-Ul-Momineen(امير المؤمنين),

151
00:12:05,847 --> 00:12:07,964
why the Khalifah(خليفه) would ask about such a simple person.)

152
00:12:08,242 --> 00:12:10,317
I mean, who is he, who is Owais Al-Qarni(إويس ألقرني)?

153
00:12:10,563 --> 00:12:15,707
Nobody knew him, except his relatives and the people who lived with him.

154
00:12:15,993 --> 00:12:18,683
And they saw him as simple, normal human being.

155
00:12:18,994 --> 00:12:21,497
He wasn't a leader of a Muslim army.

156
00:12:21,734 --> 00:12:23,748
He wasn't an Ameer(امير) of a Jama'at(جماعة),

157
00:12:24,026 --> 00:12:26,583
he wasn't a famous scholar or a Imam(امام),

158
00:12:26,858 --> 00:12:28,873
he was just a simple human being.

159
00:12:29,084 --> 00:12:32,197
But there was something in his heart that made him special,

160
00:12:32,504 --> 00:12:38,730
in fact, he was so special that Rasool Allah ﷺ told the Sahabah(صحابه),

161
00:12:39,186 --> 00:12:43,023
that when a delegation comes from Yemen from the tribe of Muraad(مراد).

162
00:12:43,381 --> 00:12:46,260
There will be man with them, his name is Owais Al-Qarni(إويس ألقرني),

163
00:12:46,624 --> 00:12:51,260
if you see him than ask him, to ask Allah to forgive you,

164
00:12:52,209 --> 00:12:55,112
this man is, so special that you should ask him for Dua(دُعَا),

165
00:12:55,366 --> 00:12:59,052
he was one of the Saliheen(صالحين) one of the Aouliyaa(أولياء) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

166
00:12:59,307 --> 00:13:01,151
and whose Rasool Allah ﷺ telling it to?

167
00:13:01,339 --> 00:13:04,588
He is telling it to the Sahaba(صحابه) the greatest generation that ever lived.

168
00:13:04,782 --> 00:13:07,181
And Owais Al-Qarni(إويس ألقرني) is not a Sahabi(صحابي), he is a Taba'ee(تابعي)

169
00:13:07,542 --> 00:13:09,188
because he never saw Rasool Allah ﷺ,

170
00:13:09,319 --> 00:13:14,175
he wanted to make Hijrah(هجرة) to Rasool Ullah but because his mother was alone and ill,

171
00:13:14,215 --> 00:13:17,962
 he stayed behind with her and Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away.

172
00:13:18,013 --> 00:13:22,927
So, he never had a chance to meet him, but Rasool Allah ﷺ knew him and talked about him.

173
00:13:23,069 --> 00:13:25,724
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) when he met with Owais Al-Qarni(إويس ألقرني) he told him,

174
00:13:26,077 --> 00:13:27,336
ask Allah to forgive me.

175
00:13:27,884 --> 00:13:32,031
Back to this competition, so Al-Aos Wal Khazraj(اَلْأوس وَالْخزْرج) would compete with each other.

176
00:13:32,503 --> 00:13:35,797
What was their competition about, it was about Al-Aakhira(آخرة),

177
00:13:36,159 --> 00:13:38,444
who would serve Rasool Allah ﷺ better,

178
00:13:38,906 --> 00:13:45,673
and in this case, it was because Al-Aos(ألأوس) had the honor of assassinating Ka'ab Ibn Ashraf(كعب إبن أشرف),

179
00:13:45,795 --> 00:13:47,490
who would defame Rasool Allah ﷺ,

180
00:13:47,752 --> 00:13:51,799
Al-Khazraj(اَلْخَزرج), didn't want to be left out on this.

181
00:13:52,034 --> 00:13:53,701
They wanted to do something similar.

182
00:13:53,871 --> 00:13:58,580
So, they had a meeting and they discussed the issue amongst themselves

183
00:13:59,078 --> 00:14:07,890
and they came up with the name of Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) as a good candidate or performing such an operation against,

184
00:14:08,476 --> 00:14:12,751
and they presented the idea to Rasool Allah ﷺ and Rasool Ullah approved it.

185
00:14:13,503 --> 00:14:22,906
Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) was the man appointed to lead this special operations group, one of Al-Khazraj(اَلْخَزرج)

186
00:14:23,413 --> 00:14:31,515
and they set out to infiltrate deep into the land of Khaybar(خيبر).

187
00:14:31,777 --> 00:14:37,754
This is before the Battle of Khaybar(خيبر) and Khaybar(خيبر) was the stronghold of the Jews.

188
00:14:37,928 --> 00:14:43,892
Nevertheless, the courage of the Sahabah(صحابه) was to lead them, deep into the land of Khaybar(خيبر)

189
00:14:43,932 --> 00:14:46,914
 and Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) lived in a fortress of his.

190
00:14:47,249 --> 00:14:51,794
He wasn't living in a normal house, he was living in a palace and it was a fortress.

191
00:14:52,327 --> 00:15:00,257
So, they marched out and they arrived at the gates of the fortress of Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) .

192
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:03,114
Now, how would they get in?

193
00:15:03,447 --> 00:15:08,566
Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) played a trick against the Yahood(يهود).

194
00:15:09,082 --> 00:15:13,157
In a narration and there are two narrations of this in Al-Bukhari(البخاري).

195
00:15:13,514 --> 00:15:18,838
In one narration it says that, these Yahood(يهود), they lost a donkey,

196
00:15:19,385 --> 00:15:25,823
so they opened the gates and some men came out to fetch out this donkey,

197
00:15:26,527 --> 00:15:31,673
Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) stood next to the wall.

198
00:15:32,058 --> 00:15:39,971
And then he sat down and covered himself, as if he was responding to the call of nature,

199
00:15:40,556 --> 00:15:44,072
pretended this in front of Al-Yahood(اليهود).

200
00:15:44,970 --> 00:15:49,053
So what they thought is that he came out from the fortress.

201
00:15:49,178 --> 00:15:55,523
Because in those days, they didn't have the restrooms inside their dwellings, they would go outside

202
00:15:56,064 --> 00:16:01,889
and they would go, far away from their houses to respond to the call of nature.

203
00:16:01,937 --> 00:16:07,487
So, they thought that he came out of the fortress to respond to the call of nature,

204
00:16:07,978 --> 00:16:09,390
so when they went in they said;

205
00:16:09,470 --> 00:16:10,404
 ياعبدالله

206
00:16:10,478 --> 00:16:14,668
o servant of Allah, if you want to come in, then now is the time.

207
00:16:15,437 --> 00:16:19,720
So, he walked in, normally, the trick that he played on them worked.

208
00:16:20,476 --> 00:16:25,373
So, now he was inside the fortress, while all of his companions were outside.

209
00:16:25,690 --> 00:16:27,952
He told them to wait outside for him.

210
00:16:28,679 --> 00:16:29,703
So, now he was in.

211
00:16:29,980 --> 00:16:35,251
He hide in a donkey stall, and he was observing the gatekeeper

212
00:16:35,949 --> 00:16:40,337
and was able to see where he would hide the keys.!

213
00:16:40,597 --> 00:16:44,494
In one narration it says: They were hung on a wooden peg

214
00:16:44,541 --> 00:16:48,146
 and another narration, it says they were in a niche, in the wall.

215
00:16:48,359 --> 00:16:56,836
Anyway Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) said, that the men went on to have dinner with Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع),

216
00:16:57,629 --> 00:17:03,685
so he remained in hiding, until all of these men left and the lights were turned off.

217
00:17:03,898 --> 00:17:05,145
It was a very dark night,

218
00:17:05,910 --> 00:17:08,447
Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) went and fetched out the keys

219
00:17:09,074 --> 00:17:12,557
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) all  of the keys were together, all of the keys for the fortress,

220
00:17:12,644 --> 00:17:18,152
the gate of the fortress and the keys for the Palace of Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع), they were all there,

221
00:17:18,628 --> 00:17:20,327
so now he had the keys with him.

222
00:17:20,813 --> 00:17:26,008
So, he would open the doors and then he would lock them from inside.

223
00:17:27,219 --> 00:17:34,034
Therefore, if anyone came in, to help Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع), he would find that the gates are closed

224
00:17:34,489 --> 00:17:39,938
and the keys are not there, so he would open every door and lock it.

225
00:17:40,898 --> 00:17:44,811
Now, this is a double edged sword, yes it would prevent people from coming in to help him,

226
00:17:45,089 --> 00:17:49,573
but it would also hinder the escape of Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق)

227
00:17:50,344 --> 00:17:51,699
but anyway, this is what he did.

228
00:17:51,984 --> 00:17:55,783
until he made it into the inner chambers of Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع).

229
00:17:56,136 --> 00:18:02,626
Now, he is with Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) in the same room and Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) is asleep, and the lights are turned off.

230
00:18:03,014 --> 00:18:05,463
 Tayyeb(طيب), How is he going to find out his location?

231
00:18:05,675 --> 00:18:06,795
He can see nothing.

232
00:18:07,316 --> 00:18:10,093
Now, what did Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) do?

233
00:18:10,578 --> 00:18:13,388
He just called out, he said: Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع).

234
00:18:13,937 --> 00:18:21,595
It takes a lot of courage to do such a thing, it's a terrifying thing, to call out for someone, in such a situation,

235
00:18:21,930 --> 00:18:28,994
but also on the other hand it's more terrifying for Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) to hear this man calling him, inside his own bedroom.

236
00:18:29,671 --> 00:18:31,978
So, Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) is calling Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع).

237
00:18:32,575 --> 00:18:34,903
Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) woke up and said: Who are you?

238
00:18:35,285 --> 00:18:36,650
Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) said;

239
00:18:36,698 --> 00:18:44,252
So I struck with my sword at the source of the voice, he can't see anything he just called him

240
00:18:44,759 --> 00:18:51,242
and the reason he did so he wanted the man to speak, so he can recognize the source of the voice and attack it,

241
00:18:51,691 --> 00:18:56,313
so he struck with his sword at the source of the voice, he said:

242
00:18:56,730 --> 00:18:57,871
فَلَمْ اُغْنِ عَنْه’ شَيْئَا

243
00:18:58,351 --> 00:19:01,982
He said: My blow was futile,

244
00:19:02,316 --> 00:19:10,950
yes he did hit him but it wasn't accurate enough strike and obviously, there's confusion in such a circumstance,

245
00:19:11,435 --> 00:19:13,238
 so it didn't kill him.

246
00:19:13,443 --> 00:19:17,361
Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع), yelled out for help, he screamed out.

247
00:19:17,726 --> 00:19:19,091
What did Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) do?

248
00:19:19,131 --> 00:19:22,520
Ya'ani Masha Allah(يعني ماشاءالله) Abdullah Bin Ateeq رضي الله عنه,

249
00:19:22,980 --> 00:19:28,274
he had very good response and intelligence on the spot, thinking on his feet,

250
00:19:28,781 --> 00:19:30,392
when Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) called out for help,

251
00:19:30,432 --> 00:19:36,496
Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق), he retreated and then he came back changing his voice

252
00:19:36,965 --> 00:19:38,915
and said:  Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) what do you need?

253
00:19:39,349 --> 00:19:44,590
Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) said: Woe on to your mother, there's a man right here and he struck me with his sword.

254
00:19:45,051 --> 00:19:47,523
So, Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) he struck him again,

255
00:19:48,293 --> 00:19:50,402
again at the source of the voice.

256
00:19:50,846 --> 00:19:53,235
Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) called out for help again,

257
00:19:53,371 --> 00:19:58,825
Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق), retreated another time came in changing his voice

258
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:01,034
 and said: Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) what do you need?

259
00:20:01,203 --> 00:20:05,636
He said: Woe on to your mother, there's a man in here, trying to kill me.

260
00:20:06,144 --> 00:20:07,958
Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) said: This time,

261
00:20:08,527 --> 00:20:10,838
I came to him and he was lying on his back.

262
00:20:11,021 --> 00:20:13,489
Now he was already struck with a sword two times,

263
00:20:13,767 --> 00:20:17,505
now he was laying on his back still alive, but laying on his back.

264
00:20:17,811 --> 00:20:18,753
 Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) said;

265
00:20:18,840 --> 00:20:27,213
This time, I thrust my sword into his stomach, until I found out the bone and then I cracked it.

266
00:20:27,809 --> 00:20:29,267
What bone are we talking about?

267
00:20:29,634 --> 00:20:31,402
He struck the spinal cord.

268
00:20:31,691 --> 00:20:35,580
So, that's it. He said: I heard the bone crack, meaning that the man is dead.

269
00:20:36,041 --> 00:20:39,399
 If the spine is broken, then it's certain death.

270
00:20:39,972 --> 00:20:43,495
So, now Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) said; I retreated.

271
00:20:44,028 --> 00:20:49,573
Now, the inner chambers, his bedroom of Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) was in the upper level

272
00:20:50,092 --> 00:20:53,130
and there was a wooden ladder that would lead up to it.

273
00:20:53,568 --> 00:20:57,920
When Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) was coming down, in this ladder or stairs.

274
00:20:58,763 --> 00:21:02,934
He said: I came down and in my confusion,

275
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:10,858
I thought that I have hit the last step of the ladder, when there was one more left,

276
00:21:11,361 --> 00:21:13,234
so he fell down and he broke his leg.

277
00:21:14,213 --> 00:21:17,078
He said and then I made it out to my companions

278
00:21:17,338 --> 00:21:20,531
and told them that, I have killed Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع).

279
00:21:21,224 --> 00:21:23,118
But Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) Subhaan Allah,

280
00:21:24,271 --> 00:21:28,791
he still wanted to make sure definitely that he is dead,

281
00:21:29,408 --> 00:21:34,842
so he told his companions, to go back and deliver the good news to Rasool Allah ﷺ

282
00:21:35,057 --> 00:21:41,396
and I'm going to hang behind and wait, until I hear the announcement of his death,

283
00:21:41,955 --> 00:21:52,667
keep in mind that he broke his leg, so he stayed behind and he heard the news of, the death of Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع).

284
00:21:53,377 --> 00:21:55,830
In the narration of Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ)

285
00:21:56,678 --> 00:22:03,267
he said: I heard his wife come to Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) and say;

286
00:22:03,476 --> 00:22:05,258
فَاضَ وَ اِلَهَ يَهُوْدْ

287
00:22:05,855 --> 00:22:09,654
He is dead in the name of the God of the Jews.

288
00:22:10,211 --> 00:22:11,718
What did Abdullah Bin Ateeq(عبدالله بن عتيق) say?

289
00:22:11,968 --> 00:22:14,221
And I want you to pay attention to his words. He said;

290
00:22:14,625 --> 00:22:21,078
And I swear, I never heard words sweeter to my ears than those.

291
00:22:21,714 --> 00:22:23,684
And we'll get back to this statement.

292
00:22:23,998 --> 00:22:25,506
Why was Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) killed?

293
00:22:25,943 --> 00:22:27,903
Ibn Hajar(إبن حجر) says;

294
00:22:28,355 --> 00:22:34,467
وَكَانَ اَبُوْ رَفِعَ يُؤذِيْ رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم وَيُعِيْنُ عَلَيْهِ،

295
00:22:34,966 --> 00:22:42,981
وَذكَرَ اَبْنُ عَائِذ مِنْ طَرِيْقِ الْاَسْوَدْ عَنْ عُرْوَةْ اَنَّه’ كَانَ مِمَّنْ اَعَانَ غَطَفَانَ و غَيْرَهُمْ مِنْ مُشْرِكِي الْعَرَبْ

296
00:22:43,275 --> 00:22:46,568
مِنْ الّمَالِ الْكَثِيْرُ، عَلَى رَسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم

297
00:22:46,879 --> 00:22:53,093
Ibn Hajar(إبن حجر) says: Abu Rafiaa(ابورافع) used to harm Rasool Allah ﷺ  and assist against him

298
00:22:53,559 --> 00:22:57,806
and Ibn Aaiz(إبن عائذ) said, that he was one of those,

299
00:22:58,442 --> 00:23:06,490
who supported the Ghatafaan(غطفان) and other polytheistic Arabs, with money to fight Rasool Allah ﷺ .

300
00:23:06,762 --> 00:23:11,516
So, his support was financial support and also by word.

301
00:23:12,523 --> 00:23:21,532
Another event that happened within this period is the assassination of Khalid Ibn Sufiyan Ibn Nubih Al-Hudhali(خالد إبن سفيان إبن نُبَيح الهذلي),

302
00:23:22,103 --> 00:23:23,293
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

303
00:23:23,617 --> 00:23:28,792
اِنَّه’ قَدْ بَلَغَنِيْ اَنَّ خالد بن سفيان بن نُبَيح الهذلي

304
00:23:29,109 --> 00:23:33,329
يَجْمَعَ لِي الْنَّاسِ لِيَغْزُونِيْ وَهُوَ بِعُرَنَة فَأتِهِ فَاقْتُلْه

305
00:23:33,578 --> 00:23:38,898
I have been informed that Khalid(خالد) is gathering a force of men to attack me,

306
00:23:39,164 --> 00:23:42,444
he is at Urana(عرانة) go to him, and kill him.

307
00:23:42,907 --> 00:23:47,679
Khalid Ibn Sufiyan(خالد إبن سفيان) was an outstanding leader of his people,

308
00:23:48,044 --> 00:23:52,247
he was one of those charismatic figures who have the ability to mobilize men

309
00:23:52,653 --> 00:23:54,516
and to make out of nothing, something.

310
00:23:55,036 --> 00:23:58,575
He was successful leader, he belong to the tribe Hudhail(هذيل),

311
00:23:58,599 --> 00:24:04,204
Hudhail(هذيل) are Bedouins in Hijaaz(حجاز) and they're famous as being very eloquent.

312
00:24:04,313 --> 00:24:06,599
قَالُوْ هُدَيْل اَشْعَرَالْعَرَبْ

313
00:24:06,959 --> 00:24:09,707
 They were the best poets of the Arabs

314
00:24:10,212 --> 00:24:13,757
and they lived on the outskirts of Makkah.

315
00:24:14,099 --> 00:24:17,928
Khalid Ibn Sufiyan(خالد إبن سفيان) was mobilizing men to fight Rasool Allah ﷺ,

316
00:24:18,239 --> 00:24:25,159
here we were in a situation, where the people were in need of a leader and the leader was Khalid Ibn Sufiyan(خالد إبن سفيان).

317
00:24:25,407 --> 00:24:29,263
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ did not see the need, to fight his army

318
00:24:29,650 --> 00:24:35,594
but to preemptively attack and get rid of Khalid Ibn Sufiyan(خالد إبن سفيان)

319
00:24:35,658 --> 00:24:38,907
because if he does so, he would avoid a lot of bloodshed.

320
00:24:39,763 --> 00:24:45,089
If Khalid Ibn Sufiyan(خالد إبن سفيان) is out of the arena, Hudhail(هذيل) are not going to fight him,

321
00:24:45,958 --> 00:24:50,370
unlike with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), the fight with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) did not depend on leadership.

322
00:24:50,856 --> 00:24:52,879
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were going to fight regardless,

323
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:54,704
when Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) was there, they fought

324
00:24:54,784 --> 00:25:01,225
and after he was killed they carried on the fight in fact the fight only became worse, after Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) was killed.

325
00:25:01,635 --> 00:25:03,802
But here at the situation was different,

326
00:25:03,882 --> 00:25:10,967
so we find that Rasool Allah ﷺ never targeted the leadership of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) with special operations to assassinate them

327
00:25:11,379 --> 00:25:14,693
but he did this with some of the leaders of Al-Yahood(اليهود)

328
00:25:15,095 --> 00:25:17,779
and he did it also with Khalid Ibn Sufiyan(خالد إبن سفيان)

329
00:25:18,024 --> 00:25:20,365
because this is going to avoid killing other people,

330
00:25:20,935 --> 00:25:28,006
it's gonna prevent, a larger battle escalating, and more war happening.

331
00:25:28,220 --> 00:25:31,334
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Go and get rid of Khalid Ibn Sufiyan(خالد إبن سفيان),

332
00:25:32,028 --> 00:25:37,775
Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس), never met, Khalid Ibn Sufiyan Al-Hudhali(خالد إبن سفيان الهذلي) in his life,

333
00:25:38,021 --> 00:25:41,807
so he told Rasool Allah ﷺ: How can I recognize him, give me a sign.

334
00:25:42,126 --> 00:25:43,701
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

335
00:25:44,294 --> 00:25:46,732
اِذَا رَاَيْتَه’شَعَرْتَ(وَجَدْتُ) لَه’قَشَعِرَيْرَةَ

336
00:25:46,819 --> 00:25:48,780
When you see him, you will shiver.

337
00:25:49,074 --> 00:25:54,171
Now, Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم) was this shiver because Khalid Ibn Sufiyan(خالد إبن سفيان) had such a great presence

338
00:25:54,688 --> 00:26:00,323
 or was is going to be a special sign, just then, for Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) to recognize him,  Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم).

339
00:26:00,458 --> 00:26:03,820
But regardless Khalid Ibn Sufiyan(خالد إبن سفيان) was a special individual.

340
00:26:04,392 --> 00:26:10,113
Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) moved out, he was alone, an army of his own.

341
00:26:10,530 --> 00:26:13,241
This is the courage that Sahaba رضي الله عنهم had,

342
00:26:13,864 --> 00:26:19,966
and he's gonna travel deep into enemy territory, in Urana(عرانة) next to Makkah,

343
00:26:20,677 --> 00:26:26,113
so he made it there and he found out the location of the army camp,

344
00:26:26,703 --> 00:26:29,985
where Khalid Ibn Sufiyan(خالد إبن سفيان) is gathering the men.

345
00:26:30,353 --> 00:26:35,782
He saw him and he felt shiver, the sign that Rasool Allah ﷺ mentioned

346
00:26:36,584 --> 00:26:40,351
and Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) said: I never shivered from anyone in my life.

347
00:26:40,871 --> 00:26:43,594
This was the first time that he ever felt such a shiver.

348
00:26:44,329 --> 00:26:48,358
It was time for As-Salaat-Ul-Asr(الصلاة العصر) and Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) said;

349
00:26:48,403 --> 00:26:53,954
وَخشِيْتُ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ بَيْنِيْ وَبَيْنَهُ مُّجَاوَلَهْ تَشْغَلْنِيْ عَنِّ(تَمْنَعْنِيْ مِنَّ) الصَّلاةْ

350
00:26:54,472 --> 00:27:02,197
He said: I feared that there might be a conflict between me and him that would prevent me from Salah(صلاة).

351
00:27:02,584 --> 00:27:07,199
Meaning this conflict could take time and wouldn't be able to pray, so what did he do

352
00:27:07,487 --> 00:27:10,728
 he prayed while he was walking towards his target.

353
00:27:10,833 --> 00:27:13,780
وَكُنْتُ اُوْمِىءُ لِلرَّكُوْعِ وَالسُّجُوْدْ بِرَأسِي

354
00:27:14,182 --> 00:27:17,615
And I would make Sujood(سجود) and Rakooh(ركوع) by movements of my head.

355
00:27:18,366 --> 00:27:20,710
So, he walked up to him and greeted him,

356
00:27:21,027 --> 00:27:22,228
Khalid Ibn Sufiyan(خالد إبن سفيان) said;

357
00:27:22,268 --> 00:27:23,019
 مَنِ الرَّجُلْ

358
00:27:23,154 --> 00:27:23,975
Who is the man.?

359
00:27:24,251 --> 00:27:28,851
قَالَ: اَنَا رَجُلٌ مِّنَّ الْعَرَبْ سَمِعَ بِكَ وَ بِجَمْعِكَ لِهَذَالرَّجُلْ

360
00:27:29,028 --> 00:27:37,084
I am a Bedouin, I'm a man from amongst the Arabs who heard about you and you're gathering a force for this man,

361
00:27:37,394 --> 00:27:37,666
 he said;

362
00:27:37,690 --> 00:27:38,568
اَنَا فِيْ ذَالِكْ

363
00:27:38,663 --> 00:27:41,081
That's what I'm doing, he said: I came to follow you,

364
00:27:41,367 --> 00:27:45,376
so then he held the conversation with him to break the ice

365
00:27:45,820 --> 00:27:51,712
and when Khalid Ibn Sufiyan(خالد إبن سفيان) was comfortable with Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس)

366
00:27:52,207 --> 00:27:54,094
and the opportune moment arrived,

367
00:27:54,538 --> 00:27:59,202
Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) struck, Khalid Ibn Sufiyan(خالد إبن سفيان) and killed him.

368
00:27:59,765 --> 00:28:01,813
He walked away and he said: Tarakat-Hoo(تَرَكَتْه’) ,

369
00:28:02,090 --> 00:28:06,140
I left him with his woman crouched over him,

370
00:28:06,777 --> 00:28:11,155
Rasool Allah ﷺ greeted Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) by saying,

371
00:28:11,179 --> 00:28:12,138
أَفْلَحَ الْوَجْه

372
00:28:12,686 --> 00:28:14,486
May your face be successful.

373
00:28:14,970 --> 00:28:15,906
Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) said;

374
00:28:15,938 --> 00:28:17,539
أَفْلَحَ الْوَجْهُكَ يَا رَسُول الله

375
00:28:17,579 --> 00:28:19,435
May your face be successful too.

376
00:28:19,765 --> 00:28:25,086
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ took him in to his house and gave him a stick.

377
00:28:25,764 --> 00:28:27,994
Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) walked out without saying a word.

378
00:28:28,527 --> 00:28:29,864
And what was the stick for?

379
00:28:30,370 --> 00:28:32,006
Why did Rasool Allah ﷺ  give it to him?

380
00:28:32,148 --> 00:28:33,613
What is he gonna do with it?

381
00:28:33,807 --> 00:28:35,720
Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس)  dare not to ask.

382
00:28:35,839 --> 00:28:41,936
They were very shy, in dealing with Rasool Allah ﷺ, so he just walked out without saying a word.

383
00:28:42,791 --> 00:28:44,751
This was the gift that Rasool Ullah gave him, a stick.

384
00:28:45,515 --> 00:28:48,892
So, his people told him, what is the stick.?

385
00:28:49,157 --> 00:28:50,561
He said: Rasool Ullah gave it to me.

386
00:28:50,648 --> 00:28:51,577
Why did they give it to you?

387
00:28:51,743 --> 00:28:52,575
He said: I don't know?

388
00:28:52,857 --> 00:28:54,280
They said: Go back and ask him!

389
00:28:54,782 --> 00:28:56,926
He went back to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

390
00:28:57,069 --> 00:29:00,041
O Rasool Ullah, Why did you give me the stick?

391
00:29:00,379 --> 00:29:00,982
He said;

392
00:29:01,266 --> 00:29:08,300
آيَةً تَكُوْنُ بَيْنِيْ وَبَيْنَكَ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةْ اِنَّا اَقَلَّ النَّاسِ يَوْمَئِذٍ اَلْمُتَخَصِّرُوْنَ

393
00:29:08,844 --> 00:29:12,927
He said this is a sign between me and you on the Day of Judgment,

394
00:29:13,689 --> 00:29:17,489
there will be very few that day, with something, to lean upon.

395
00:29:18,052 --> 00:29:20,286
Rasool Ullah gave him the stick as a gift,

396
00:29:21,111 --> 00:29:25,771
so that on the Day of Judgment it will be a sign between him and Rasool Ullah.

397
00:29:26,624 --> 00:29:31,368
Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) coupled that stick with his sword, he kept it with his sword,

398
00:29:31,990 --> 00:29:37,363
and then in his will, he asked that, the stick be buried with him.

399
00:29:38,036 --> 00:29:41,056
So, it was put inside his coffin with him,

400
00:29:41,571 --> 00:29:47,801
so that on the Day of Judgment, when he's resurrected, he will pick up that stick and go to Rasool Allah ﷺ

401
00:29:48,276 --> 00:29:52,444
and it will be a sign between him and Rasool Ullah, on that very difficult day,

402
00:29:52,829 --> 00:29:55,707
when there will be very few people with something to lean upon.

403
00:29:56,178 --> 00:29:59,230
And this Rawayah(رواية) is in Masnad Imam Ahmad(مسند اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ).

404
00:30:00,110 --> 00:30:03,666
One important lesson, brothers and sisters from this story,

405
00:30:04,122 --> 00:30:05,251
The importance of Salah(صلاة),

406
00:30:05,720 --> 00:30:11,988
the thing that concerned, Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس), when he was walking towards Khalid Ibn Sufiyan(خالد إبن سفيان) was Salaat-Ul-Asr(صلاةالعصر).

407
00:30:12,480 --> 00:30:15,321
And the thing that concerned, the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم,

408
00:30:15,364 --> 00:30:20,325
when Rasool Ullah, was talking to them about the signs of the end of time, when he was talking about Ad-Dajjal(الدجال)

409
00:30:20,622 --> 00:30:23,204
and that one day of Ad-Dajjal(الدجال), will be like a year,

410
00:30:23,658 --> 00:30:24,992
what did the Sahabah(صحابه) say?

411
00:30:25,182 --> 00:30:28,482
How is that explained, physically?

412
00:30:28,754 --> 00:30:33,401
Can you give us the astronomy explanation of how that is possible?

413
00:30:33,957 --> 00:30:35,171
What did they say? They said;

414
00:30:35,625 --> 00:30:37,194
هَلْ تَكْفِيْنَا فِيْهِ صَلَاةَ يَوْمْ

415
00:30:37,536 --> 00:30:43,278
Is it's enough for us to pray in that day, the five daily prayers, prayers of one day?

416
00:30:43,692 --> 00:30:45,031
They were thinking about Salah(صلاة),

417
00:30:45,547 --> 00:30:50,222
and Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن انيس) in this life and death situation,

418
00:30:50,563 --> 00:30:56,231
in this confusing situation, a person in that situation would be perplexed,

419
00:30:56,381 --> 00:30:59,991
and as we just said, that his body shivered when he saw this man,

420
00:31:00,389 --> 00:31:05,169
but, Salah(صلاة), Salah(صلاة), Salah(صلاة) he prayed, walking towards him.

421
00:31:05,794 --> 00:31:09,014
Brothers and Sisters, there's no excuse in leaving Salah(صلاة)

422
00:31:09,600 --> 00:31:13,076
if you don't have money, you're excused from paying Zakat(زكواة).

423
00:31:13,551 --> 00:31:18,044
If you're ill, you're excused from fasting and you can play a Fidyah(فدية) instead.

424
00:31:18,369 --> 00:31:23,973
If you don't have the financial ability and the road to Hajj(حَجْ) is not safe

425
00:31:24,408 --> 00:31:25,969
you don't have to make Hajj(حَجْ),

426
00:31:26,393 --> 00:31:31,616
 but there is no situation in which a Muslim is excused from Salah(صلاة).

427
00:31:32,023 --> 00:31:38,005
Even in the battlefield, we have to pray and we're given the Fiqh(فقه) of it, in Salaat-Ul-Khauf(صلاة الخوف).

428
00:31:38,699 --> 00:31:41,738
In fact, the Sahabah(صحابه) considered Salah(صلاة) to be so important.

429
00:31:41,985 --> 00:31:47,579
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) used to say; that if a Muslim leaves one Salah(صلاة) intentionally then he has disbelieved.

430
00:31:48,032 --> 00:31:53,191
We know that after that Ulema(علماء) discussed the issue of the Kuffr(كفر) of Taarik-Us-Salah(تارك الصلاة),

431
00:31:53,255 --> 00:31:56,025
 whether the one who leaves Salah(صلاة) is Kafir(كافر) or not

432
00:31:56,406 --> 00:31:59,651
and one can go back to the books Fiqh(فقه) to see, what they said about that?

433
00:31:59,942 --> 00:32:03,852
 It's the opinion of Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) that if the person leaves it out of laziness,

434
00:32:04,177 --> 00:32:07,200
 than he is a Kafir(كافر), while the other Ulema(علماء) said;

435
00:32:07,696 --> 00:32:10,690
that Muslims Kafir(كافر) only, if he leaves it intentionally.

436
00:32:10,912 --> 00:32:17,535
Anyway this is not the place to discuss this issue but, it's very important, it's the most important Ibadah(عبادة),

437
00:32:17,794 --> 00:32:21,019
so we should never dismiss our Salah(صلاة)

438
00:32:21,361 --> 00:32:27,637
and for those Muslims because of their employment, leave for example Salat-Ul-Jum'ah(صلاةالجمعه),

439
00:32:27,931 --> 00:32:33,806
or they leave some Salawaat(صلوات), we say to them, It'taqillah(إتقى الله), Fear Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

440
00:32:34,042 --> 00:32:38,550
 Abdullah Bin Unais(عبدالله بن أنيس), in this situation that is more important than your employment,

441
00:32:38,845 --> 00:32:44,473
more dangerous than your situation, and he did not leave Salah(صلاة), so we should never leave Salah(صلاة).

442
00:32:45,663 --> 00:32:52,574
Next event that happened within this period is regarding Zainab Bint Jahash(زينب بنت جحش).

443
00:32:53,163 --> 00:32:57,768
Zainab Bint Jahash رضي الله عنها, Al-Assadiyyah(ألاَسَدِيْةَ) from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

444
00:32:58,451 --> 00:33:00,835
She was the sister of Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش),

445
00:33:01,020 --> 00:33:04,941
and we talked about his story in the earlier lectures

446
00:33:05,465 --> 00:33:10,663
and her mother is Umaimah Bint Abdul-Muttalib(عميمه بنت عبدالمطلب), the sister of Hamza(حمزه),

447
00:33:11,224 --> 00:33:16,848
so her mother is the aunt of Rasool Ullah, which makes her, his cousin.

448
00:33:17,152 --> 00:33:31,195
Zainab Bint Jahash رضي الله عنها, Rasool Allah ﷺ visited her and he proposed to her marriage to his adopted son,

449
00:33:31,436 --> 00:33:32,994
Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه).

450
00:33:33,227 --> 00:33:35,073
Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) was a slave.

451
00:33:35,234 --> 00:33:41,751
And he's asking, Zainab Bint Jahash(زينب بنت جحش), who comes from the nobility of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) to marry a slave.

452
00:33:42,150 --> 00:33:48,861
 Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to break the barriers of discrimination and racism that existed

453
00:33:49,311 --> 00:33:52,771
and he wanted to start among his own family

454
00:33:53,129 --> 00:33:58,682
and ask that Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) marry his own cousin Zainab Bint Jahash(زينب بنت جحش).

455
00:33:59,014 --> 00:33:59,922
She said: No,

456
00:34:00,339 --> 00:34:02,464
He(ﷺ) said: Yes, you will marry her.

457
00:34:02,607 --> 00:34:09,597
 She said: O Messenger of Allah, let me think about it and while they were talking, the Ayah(آية) was revealed,

458
00:34:09,945 --> 00:34:23,633
وَمَا كَانَ لِمُؤْمِنٍ وَلَا مُؤْمِنَةٍ إِذَا قَضَى اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَمْرًا أَنْ يَكُونَ لَهُمُ الْخِيَرَةُ مِنْ أَمْرِهِمْ ۗ

459
00:34:24,024 --> 00:34:31,784
وَمَنْ يَعْصِ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ ضَلَالًا مُبِينًا۝

460
00:34:32,299 --> 00:34:39,967
"It is not fitting for a believer, man or woman when a matter has been decided by Allah

461
00:34:40,255 --> 00:34:44,135
and His Messenger to have any option about their decision,

462
00:34:44,597 --> 00:34:50,224
if anyone disobeys Allah and His Messenger, he is indeed on a clearly wrong path.

463
00:34:50,787 --> 00:34:56,360
If our desires are contrary to something that Rasool Allah ﷺ wants us to do,

464
00:34:56,631 --> 00:34:59,516
we still do what Rasool Allah ﷺ wants us to do.

465
00:35:00,205 --> 00:35:03,583
And it's important that we don't follow our whims and desires

466
00:35:03,764 --> 00:35:05,796
but we follow the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

467
00:35:05,935 --> 00:35:08,161
what excuse do we have in not following His Sunnah(سنة).

468
00:35:08,681 --> 00:35:12,790
What excuse, Do we have in not following the law of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, just because we don't like it,

469
00:35:13,284 --> 00:35:17,017
just because it didn't suit our Ahwa'a(اَهْوَاء), our whims and desires.

470
00:35:17,738 --> 00:35:22,328
We are slaves of Allahعَزّوجَلّ and we are followers of Muhammadﷺ

471
00:35:22,582 --> 00:35:26,987
and whatever, we are told to do, we do it's not up to us,

472
00:35:27,958 --> 00:35:30,522
so Zainab Bint Jahash(زينب بنت جحش), when this Ayah(آية) was revealed,

473
00:35:30,848 --> 00:35:34,686
she said: I accept him as a husband.

474
00:35:35,694 --> 00:35:38,762
لَا اَعْصِيْ رَسُوْل الله وَقَدْ زَوَجْتَه’ نَفْسِيْ

475
00:35:38,864 --> 00:35:42,951
I will not disobey Rasool Allah ﷺ and I marry him myself.

476
00:35:43,940 --> 00:35:47,688
But Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) things didn't work out, there was no compatibility,

477
00:35:48,051 --> 00:35:50,619
after a year they were divorced.

478
00:35:51,314 --> 00:35:55,540
Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) was coming to Rasool Allah ﷺ and complaining about his wife.

479
00:35:55,667 --> 00:35:58,335
He wasn't happy with her and she wasn't happy with him.

480
00:35:58,972 --> 00:36:00,445
But Rasool Allah ﷺ would told him;

481
00:36:00,485 --> 00:36:03,149
 اِتَّقِ اللهَ وَ اَمْسِكْ عَلَيْكَ زَوْجَكْ

482
00:36:03,366 --> 00:36:09,626
He said: Fear Allah and keep your wife, but things just couldn't continue on.

483
00:36:10,237 --> 00:36:15,602
So, divorce was a must and the marriage was ended after a year.

484
00:36:16,175 --> 00:36:24,486
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ married her and that caused the storm of talk against Rasool Allah ﷺ.

485
00:36:24,986 --> 00:36:31,993
In Arabia It was a no-no for a man to marry the wife of his adopted son.

486
00:36:32,513 --> 00:36:36,763
Adoption was serious than, this before it was made Haram(حرام) in Islam.

487
00:36:37,263 --> 00:36:40,953
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ adopted Zaid(زيد) and he was called Zaid Ibn Muhammad(زيد ابن محمد).

488
00:36:41,362 --> 00:36:47,032
So, now, all of the rules of Sharia(شريعة) that apply between a son and his father

489
00:36:47,500 --> 00:36:51,562
 applied between Muhammadﷺ and his son Zaid(زيد).

490
00:36:52,454 --> 00:36:59,542
And one of the rules that existed in those days is that a man can never married the wife of his adopted son.

491
00:36:59,860 --> 00:37:03,701
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ wanted to break this tradition among the Arabs

492
00:37:04,016 --> 00:37:09,097
and what better way to do so, than Rasool Allah ﷺ breaking that rule himself.

493
00:37:09,488 --> 00:37:15,289
It carries more weight, when Rasool Allah ﷺ does it, then when he speaks about it.

494
00:37:15,926 --> 00:37:18,845
So, now Rasool Allah ﷺ married Zainab Bint Jahash(زينب بنت جحش).

495
00:37:19,617 --> 00:37:25,072
There were two rulings here, the first ruling is that there's no more adoption

496
00:37:25,394 --> 00:37:31,190
and second ruling is that a man can marry the wife of his formerly adopted son.

497
00:37:31,388 --> 00:37:32,540
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

498
00:37:32,838 --> 00:37:38,906
مَا جَعَلَ اللَّهُ لِرَجُلٍ مِنْ قَلْبَيْنِ فِي جَوْفِهِ ۚ

499
00:37:39,255 --> 00:37:49,398
وَمَا جَعَلَ أَزْوَاجَكُمُ اللَّائِي تُظَاهِرُونَ مِنْهُنَّ أُمَّهَاتِكُمْ ۚ

500
00:37:49,889 --> 00:37:55,558
وَمَا جَعَلَ أَدْعِيَاءَكُمْ أَبْنَاءَكُمْ ۚ

501
00:37:55,844 --> 00:38:05,200
ذَٰلِكُمْ قَوْلُكُمْ بِأَفْوَاهِكُمْ ۖ وَاللَّهُ يَقُولُ الْحَقَّ وَهُوَ يَهْدِي السَّبِيلَ۝

502
00:38:05,955 --> 00:38:11,457
"Allah has not made for any man two hearts in his body, nor has He made your wives

503
00:38:11,748 --> 00:38:14,586
whom you divorce by the Izhaar(إظهار), Your mother's

504
00:38:14,745 --> 00:38:22,113
nor has He made your adopted sons your son's, such is only your manner of speech by your mouth

505
00:38:22,462 --> 00:38:25,503
 but Allah tells you, the truth and he shows the right way.

506
00:38:25,978 --> 00:38:32,318
اُدْعُوهُمْ لِآبَائِهِمْ هُوَ أَقْسَطُ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ ۚ

507
00:38:32,572 --> 00:38:41,459
فَإِنْ لَمْ تَعْلَمُوا آبَاءَهُمْ فَإِخْوَانُكُمْ فِي الدِّينِ وَمَوَالِيكُمْ ۚ

508
00:38:41,903 --> 00:38:52,048
وَلَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ فِيمَا أَخْطَأْتُمْ بِهِ وَلَٰكِنْ مَا تَعَمَّدَتْ قُلُوبُكُمْ ۚ

509
00:38:52,476 --> 00:38:56,445
وَكَانَ اللَّهُ غَفُورًا رَحِيمًا۝

510
00:38:57,435 --> 00:38:59,666
"Call them by the names of their fathers

511
00:39:00,037 --> 00:39:04,534
This is just her in the sight of Allah but if you know not their fathers names,

512
00:39:04,628 --> 00:39:07,740
call them your brothers in faith, or your Moula's

513
00:39:08,084 --> 00:39:11,562
but there is no blame on you, if you make a mistake there in.

514
00:39:11,854 --> 00:39:17,055
What counts is the intention of your hearts and Allah is oft-forgiving most merciful."

515
00:39:17,486 --> 00:39:19,775
Now just want to make a clarification here,

516
00:39:20,040 --> 00:39:25,482
what is meant by adoption here is not the meaning that we know of adoption today,

517
00:39:25,778 --> 00:39:29,594
when you adopt an orphan, no that's something very good to do it's very reward able.

518
00:39:29,862 --> 00:39:30,827
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

519
00:39:30,871 --> 00:39:33,007
أنا وكافل اليتيم كهاتين في الجنة

520
00:39:33,276 --> 00:39:38,847
Rasool Allah ﷺ says, that I will be a neighbor of the one, who sponsors the orphan.

521
00:39:39,223 --> 00:39:41,531
The adoption that is not allowed in Islam

522
00:39:41,887 --> 00:39:49,287
is where the adopted son or daughter, carries the family name of, the ones who adopt them.

523
00:39:49,688 --> 00:39:59,003
In Islam we must carry the names of our ancestors and not carry the names of the ones, who have adopted us.

524
00:39:59,829 --> 00:40:04,083
So, this is just a clarification because the word adoption in English might carry different meaning.

525
00:40:04,422 --> 00:40:07,667
Zainab Bint Jahash(زينب بنت جحش) was a very righteous woman. In fact,

526
00:40:08,187 --> 00:40:11,046
she among the wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

527
00:40:11,331 --> 00:40:15,592
she held the very important status with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

528
00:40:16,051 --> 00:40:18,408
Ayesha رضي الله عنها says;

529
00:40:18,646 --> 00:40:24,292
None of the wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ used to compete with me, in my status with Rasool Allah ﷺ but Zainab(زينب)

530
00:40:24,832 --> 00:40:27,586
and Rasool Allah ﷺ said, about her.

531
00:40:27,721 --> 00:40:30,776
أسرعكن لحاقاً بي أطولكن يداً

532
00:40:31,110 --> 00:40:38,993
The fastest among you to die after me, will be the one of you with the longest arm,

533
00:40:39,531 --> 00:40:44,801
so Ayesha(عائشه) used to say; We the wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ, would measure our arms

534
00:40:45,123 --> 00:40:50,812
to see who has the longest arm but they didn't understand, what Rasool Allah ﷺ meant?

535
00:40:51,318 --> 00:40:54,010
What he meant by this, by longest arm,

536
00:40:54,324 --> 00:41:01,262
is not literally but it means the one who gives out Sadaqah(صدقه) the most

537
00:41:01,708 --> 00:41:06,101
and that was Zainab Bint Jahash(زينب بنت جحش) and she was the one who died,

538
00:41:06,679 --> 00:41:10,966
the fastest among the wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ, after Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away.

539
00:41:11,316 --> 00:41:12,690
Ayesha(عائشه) said about her;

540
00:41:13,117 --> 00:41:18,123
لم أر امرأة قط خيراً في الدين من زينب، وأتقى لله،

541
00:41:18,210 --> 00:41:27,110
 وأصدق حديثاً، وأوصل للرحم، وأعظم صدقة، وأشد ابتذالاً لنفسها في العمل الذي تصدق به وتقربه إلى الله تعالى

542
00:41:27,490 --> 00:41:31,141
 ما عدا سورة من حدة كانت فيها، تسرع منها الفيئة

543
00:41:31,571 --> 00:41:35,011
She said: I never seen a woman better than her in her religion,

544
00:41:35,748 --> 00:41:40,941
and more fearful of Allah than her, and more truthful in her speech,

545
00:41:41,361 --> 00:41:45,723
and more attentive to the family relationships than her

546
00:41:46,223 --> 00:41:50,669
and I've never seen a woman who used to give more Sadaqah(صدقه) than her

547
00:41:51,273 --> 00:41:56,804
and she would give herself totally to the deed that she would be doing.

548
00:41:57,366 --> 00:42:00,822
And the only thing with her is that she had a temper,

549
00:42:01,264 --> 00:42:08,422
but she would very soon come back to her normal state, رضي الله عنها.

550
00:42:09,011 --> 00:42:11,614
This marriage of Rasool Allah ﷺ to Zainab(زينب)

551
00:42:12,385 --> 00:42:15,940
has been a point of controversy with the Kuffar(كفار).

552
00:42:16,638 --> 00:42:21,353
They try to use it, as an attacking point against Rasool Allah ﷺ.

553
00:42:22,034 --> 00:42:25,741
And it's interesting to see that there are two particular marriages

554
00:42:26,412 --> 00:42:30,167
that, the Kuffar(كفار) speak about the most

555
00:42:30,608 --> 00:42:36,033
and that is the marriage to Ayesha(عائشه) because of her young age and the marriage to Zainab(زينب)

556
00:42:36,522 --> 00:42:39,011
because they surrounded it with many tales and legends.

557
00:42:39,276 --> 00:42:44,740
And it's interesting to see that these are the particular two marriages that were commanded by Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

558
00:42:45,077 --> 00:42:48,605
Because Zainab bint Jahash(زينب بن جحش) would say, to the other wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ

559
00:42:48,629 --> 00:42:53,018
you are married by your parents, while I was married by Allah from on top seven Heavens.

560
00:42:53,811 --> 00:42:55,506
Because Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in Qur'an;

561
00:42:55,561 --> 00:42:56,894
 فَزَوَّجْنَاكَهَا

562
00:42:56,974 --> 00:42:58,966
We married we married her, to you.

563
00:42:59,458 --> 00:43:06,009
So Rasool Allah ﷺ when he was married to Ayesha(عائشه) there was no Aqad(عقد) or anything, he just walked in, to her room

564
00:43:06,228 --> 00:43:08,982
because the marriage was performed by Allahعَزّوجَلّ

565
00:43:09,627 --> 00:43:14,954
and with Ayesha رضي الله عنها, it happened because he has seen her in a dream

566
00:43:15,231 --> 00:43:17,559
 and we know that the dreams of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) are Wahii(وحي).

567
00:43:18,294 --> 00:43:20,712
So, that is the marriage of Rasool Allah ﷺ to Zainab(زينب).

568
00:43:21,184 --> 00:43:28,226
Also in this period Rasool Allah ﷺ married to Habibah Bint Abi Sufiyan(حبيبه بنت أبي سفيان) the daughter of Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان).

569
00:43:28,347 --> 00:43:30,147
She was in Al-Habasha(ألحبشه) at that time.

570
00:43:30,491 --> 00:43:33,109
She was with the Muhajireen(مهاجرين) in Abyssinia

571
00:43:33,632 --> 00:43:36,633
and her husband Obaidillah Bin Jahash(عبيدالله بن جحش),

572
00:43:37,117 --> 00:43:39,919
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), he was one of the Muhajireen(مهاجرين)

573
00:43:40,029 --> 00:43:43,308
but he had a change of heart, he was deceived by Shaytaan(شيطان),

574
00:43:43,689 --> 00:43:46,085
he became a Murtadd(مرتد) and became a Christian

575
00:43:46,403 --> 00:43:55,184
and he used to make fun of the Muslims and say you are looking with half of your eyes open, while I have seen the light.

576
00:43:55,509 --> 00:43:59,702
 He is referring to Christianity, he died as a Murtadd(مرتد).

577
00:44:00,121 --> 00:44:05,844
After he passed away, Rasool Allah ﷺ sent Amr Bin Umayyah Ad-Dhamri(عمرو بن أمية أضَّمْرِيْ) to An-Najjashi(ألنجاشي)

578
00:44:06,198 --> 00:44:12,129
to marry him to Habibah Bint Abi Sufiyaan(حبيبه بنت إبي سفيان) and the marriage was performed

579
00:44:12,601 --> 00:44:18,560
the Walli(وَلِّي) of Habiba(حبيبه) was her cousin, Khalid Bin Saeed Al-Aas(خالد بن سعيد بن العاص)

580
00:44:18,876 --> 00:44:23,826
 and the representative of Rasool Allah ﷺ in performing the contract was An-Najjashi(ألنجاشي)

581
00:44:24,104 --> 00:44:29,621
and by this, Umm Habibah(أم حبيبه) became Umm Ul-Mo'mineen(أم المؤمنين)

582
00:44:29,991 --> 00:44:38,382
and Muawiyah رضي الله عنه became the uncle of Al-Mo'mineen(ألمؤمنين) because he is her brother,

583
00:44:39,124 --> 00:44:44,061
رضي الله عنه وعنها والارض الله عزوجل جَميع الصحابه

584
00:44:44,204 --> 00:44:49,226
وَ صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

